```text
Sweetgrass Planned Unit Development
Page 6
Standards & Guidelines (4th Amendment)
Section 3 - Development Standards & Guidelines

Dated: 7/17/2023 RESUBMITTAL DRAFT
(Replaces corresponding UDC Section 6.4: External Lighting where applicable)
(Replaces corresponding UDC Section 4.3: Transportation Networks and Street Designs)
Section 3: Development Standards & Guidelines
A. Access Standards and Street Sections
(Replaces Corresponding UDC Section UDC §4.3.4)
1. Alternative Street Sections
a. Because of the size of Sweetgrass, its rural character, and the goal of reducing public infrastructure and
associated maintenance costs, this PUD contains alternative public street sections to the City’s UDC
street standards (UDC §4.3). Street sections allowed in Sweetgrass are illustrated in PUD Appendix A.
b. The Sweetgrass Street Sections may be adjusted slightly with concurrence from a Wyoming licensed
engineer without amending this PUD or necessitating a formal Waiver to Subdivision Standards.
2.
Residential Access and Street Standards:

a. Access to Residential Parcels: Because Sweetgrass is a series of neighborhoods designed within a planned
collector street network around a significant open space system, the access guidelines contained within
UDC §4.3.3.f.3(a) – (d) are not applicable. Residential development parcels shall provide access sufficient
for emergency vehicles (per International Fire Code, as adopted by the City when the final plat for the
residential parcel is submitted), with a minimum Level of Service of “C.”
b. SFD Residential Neighborhoods: Streets shall be dedicated public Right-of-Way (R/W) per UDC “Standard
Roadway: Residential”, unless otherwise provided for herein.
c. Non-SFD Residential Neighborhoods: Streets and drives providing access to internal parking and garages,
including alleys, may be privately owned and maintained.
d. Any alleys proposed shall be constructed to UDC§4.3 Context-based Roadway: Alley or other standard to
be approved on a case-by-case basis by the City Engineer.
e. A parcel, or a portion of a parcel within the PUD may be gated, subject to the approval of the Cheyenne
Fire Department and any applicable conditions deemed appropriate by the Fire Chief or their designee.
f. Any gated streets will be privately maintained.
g. Alternative street sections may be approved by the Committee on a case-by-case basis with concurrence
by the City Engineer and Fire Department without requiring an amendment to this PUD.

3. Non-Residential Access and Street Standards:
(Replaces Corresponding UDC Section 4.3.3)
a. SEE APPENDIX A - Sweetgrass PUD Street Sections and Standards, and
b. All applicable provisions of Section 3.A.2 above.
B. Signs, Fences, Entry Monuments and Retaining Walls
(Supplements Corresponding UDC Section 6.5: Signs and Replaces UDC Section 5.8.4 Fences)
1. Fencing will be enforced exclusively by the Design Review Committee (DRC).
2. Should the DRC default or disband, the fencing regulations of the City of Cheyenne’s Unified Development
Code shall apply and shall be enforced by the City.
3. Signage: Unless superseded herein or by an approved detailed sign program for the entire PUD and/or specific
parcels therein., signage shall be governed by UDC Section 6.5 (Signs) and Cheyenne City Municipal Ordinance(s).
a. Residential Parcels shall be governed by standards defined for UDC MR - Medium-Density Residential, and
b. Non-Residential Parcels shall be governed by standards defined for UDC CB – Community Business.
UDC Section 6.5 (Signs) and applicable Cheyenne City Municipal Ordinance(s) shall govern, unless superseded
by an approved detailed sign program for the entire PUD and/or specific parcels therein.
